From 5cd9bd01614bc56ce2576ba0ac93a28937b7e2d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:46:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): client-side sync seams behind
 kanban.sync.enabled (off) [daveey]

Phase 1 of the central Kanban sync service (hermes-mods
core/kanban-central-service.md, "proposed patch 0193"). New sibling
hermes_cli/kanban_db_sync.py holds the logic; each seam is one call.

- Config gate: kanban.sync.enabled (default false) read at first connect.
  Off: no sync table or trigger is created and stale capture triggers are
  dropped, so every kanban path behaves as before.
- On: kanban_sync_state/outbox/tombstones, uid columns, lease mirror, and
  AFTER INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE triggers that capture synced columns into the
  outbox inside the writer's transaction. Triggers are generated from
  PRAGMA table_info minus the declared local-only set; undeclared_columns()
  plus a test guard against trigger drift. BLOB cells travel as
  {"$blob": hex} so a trigger never fails a write.
- apply_remote_changes: one txn per page, echo suppression (applying flag
  + client_op_id), run_uid -> local run id, local-only columns never
  written, cursor atomic with rows, hooks fire once after commit with
  remote=True/origin_gateway, dispatcher wake.
- Leases (mode primary only): claim_task/claim_review_task ask an
  injectable client before the CAS; no grant -> claim_deferred, card stays
  ready. heartbeat_claim renews at most once per ttl/3 and bounds the claim
  at lease_expires - 60s; release_stale_claims stops a worker that lost
  its lease (run outcome lease_lost). reclaim_task releases the lease.
- delete on a synced board writes one delete op + tombstone; synced
  boards mint 16-hex time-ordered task ids.
- Gateway dispatcher sleep ends early on a sync wake.

Size ratchet offset: pure worker-context helpers moved to
kanban_db_context.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
